      {
        "id": 82688,
        "name": "Medic-Tank",
        "username": "Medic-Tank",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/medic-tank/{size}/2107_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-27T19:37:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ronway's description sounds like how my randomizer works.&nbsp; No hero should have any greater chance of appearing in the final list than any other, regardless of how many alt versions they have, and you will never see two alt version of the same hero in the results either.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I use the randomizer of this guy and use the added twist that you get the hero by seat order for added challenge and variety. Then we decide if the line up can handle avanced game against the villain that comes out. We also made an exeption where you choose wich bunker you use cause it really sucks to have engine of war against a villain without ongoings.</p>",
